        "event": "Dense Fog Advisory",
        "headline": "Dense Fog Advisory issued October 4 at 10:03PM AKDT until October 5 at 10:00AM AKDT by NWS Anchorage AK",
        "description": "* WHAT...Visibility as low as one quarter mile in dense fog.\n\n* WHERE...Central Copper Valley and Western Copper Valley.\n\n* WHEN...Until 10 AM AKDT Monday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Hazardous driving conditions due to low visibility.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...Fog, in combination with temperatures near\nfreezing, may result in slippery road conditions and patchy black\nice.",
        "severity": "Moderate",
        "certainty": "Likely",
        "urgency": "Expected",
        "sender": "NWS Anchorage AK",
        "effective": "2026-10-04T22:03:00-08:00",
        "expires": "2026-10-05T10:00:00-08:00",
        "areas": "Western Copper Valley; Central Copper Valley",
        "category": "Met",
        "response": "Execute",
        "instruction": "A dense fog advisory means visibilities will frequently be reduced to\nless than one quarter mile. If driving, slow down, use your\nheadlights, and leave plenty of distance ahead of you.",
        "lat": null,
        "lng": null
      },
      {
        "id": "urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.76b5af7e208e69622fda95c7825ee69556aefbaf.001.1",
        "event": "Special Weather Statement",
        "headline": "Special Weather Statement issued October 4 at 7:50PM AKDT by NWS Anchorage AK",
        "description": "Areas of locally dense fog will persist along portions of the\nGlenn and Richardson Highways, especially from Glennallen west to\nMendeltna, this evening through early Monday morning.\n\nPeriods of a wintry mix of precipitation are also expected across\nthe Copper River Basin through Monday morning. With temperatures\naround freezing for most locations, any precipitation may fall as\na mix of rain, snow, and freezing drizzle. Little to no\nsignificant snow and ice accumulation is expected. However, the\n",
